# Settings for one demo partner. Server-side only: none use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, so they
# never reach the browser. On your own laptop with the local chain none are needed: each
# partner falls back to the API's public local defaults.
#
# Each partner is its own copy of the app, so each needs its own values. Keep them in one file
# per partner (for example .env.bank and .env.wallet, never committed) and load that file for
# that partner's run only:
#   (set -a; . demo-bank/.env.wallet; set +a; pnpm --filter @mohar/demo-bank dev:wallet)
# A .env.local would be read by BOTH partners, so do not put these in .env.local.

# Which partner this copy plays: bank (Moher Bank, the default) or wallet (Moher Wallet).
# DEMO_PARTNER=bank

# MOHAR_API_URL=http://localhost:4000
# This partner's API key: its entry in the API's PARTNER_API_KEYS.
# MOHAR_API_KEY=
# This partner's webhook secret: its entry in the API's PARTNER_WEBHOOK_SECRETS.
# MOHAR_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# MOHAR's operator key (the API's DEV_API_KEY), only for the demo panel's price buttons.
# MOHAR_DEV_KEY=
# Signs the session cookie. Any long random string; required anywhere but your own laptop.
# SESSION_SECRET=
